<title>USA: U.S. crop production Nov 12 highlights - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. crop production Nov 12 highlights - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA Tuesday raised its 1996 corn crop estimate to 9.265 billion bushels and soybeans to 2.403 billion bushels, above analysts' expectations.</p>
<p>Last month USDA pegged corn harvest at 9.012 billion bushels and soybeans at 2.346 billion. Analysts estimated corn output at an average 9.149 billion bushels and soybeans at 2.376 billion.</p>
<p>USDA also raised ending stocks for corn to 1.107 billion bushels, more than double a year ago but almost 30 percent below 1994/95. Soybean exports were raised to 870 million bushels and ending stocks to 210 million. Wheat exports were raised to 950 million bushels and end stocks cut to 435 million bushels.  </p>
<p> -	  PRODUCTION (1,000 bushels):	YIELD/ACRE (bu):</p>
<p> -		1996----Prev.96	1995    1996-Rev.from  1995</p>
<p> Corn     9,265,288  9,012,148  7,373,876  126.5  123.0  113.5</p>
<p> Soybean  2,402,610  2,346,220  2,176,814   37.9   37.0   35.3</p>
<p> Cotton-X  18,594.1   18,189.1   17,899.8    698    673    537</p>
<p> AllWheat 2,281,763		 2,182,591   36.3	    35.8</p>
<p>X-Cotton production in 1,000 bales, yield in lbs per acre.</p>
<p>Note--Wheat data carried forward from previous forecast.  </p>
